From: Tushar Ganatra <tganatra@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Jul 2025 11:26:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: qualcomm: add EIP full-inline IPsec

Carry exact outbound XFRM state into hardware actions. Let Qualcomm PPE
bind clear-text flows to an EIP provider. Program service code 42 for
PPE-to-EIP inner-flow encapsulation, retain provider module and object
references for each PPE row, and expose the state through debugfs.

Keep virtual-port carrier and flow teardown ordered, and drain provider
objects before stopping the exported EIP API. SoCs advertise inner-flow
support independently through device tree.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/tree/87bb9b326dfe7ddafb2cc8bc588e74d552a2a9b5
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/commit/45345c1d377f42a3aac8dd9a486a2f1241a35c85
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/169bf594df03ac4b29e0ccd3f6f87e70f0f3fb6e
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/39c0281b98922dcda04f91e30dd15bccbb0896ae
Signed-off-by: Tushar Ganatra <tganatra@qti.qualcomm.com>
